%!PS
% SPDX-FileCopyrightText: 2026 EfterScript contributors
% SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
% expect-output: /undefinedresult
% expect-output: 3.0
% expect-output: 6
% Scenario: an error in the paint procedure propagates as that error
% and leaves the graphics state as it was before the paint; the
% painting operator's operands stay on the stack under the ones the
% failing operator left.
/P << /PatternType 1 /PaintType 1 /TilingType 1 /BBox [0 0 10 10]
  /XStep 10 /YStep 10 /PaintProc { pop 9 setlinewidth 1 0 div } >>
  matrix makepattern def
3 setlinewidth
P setpattern
{ 0 0 100 100 rectfill } stopped pop
$error /errorname get ==
currentlinewidth =
count =
